.TH CLAUDE-USAGE 1 "October 2026" "claude-usage @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude-usage \- Claude usage limits in your system tray
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-usage
[\fB\-\-background\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows how much of your Claude session and weekly usage limits you have left, as a
progress ring and countdown in the system tray. Opening the tray menu or running
\fBclaude-usage\fR again brings up a panel with weekly limits, per-model limits and
the context window of your most recent Claude Code session.
.PP
Running the command while the app is already running opens its panel.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start in the tray without opening the panel. Used by the "Start at login" setting.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Log debugging information to standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/claude-usage/settings.json
Preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.config/claude-usage/credentials.json
Sign-in tokens, only when no desktop keyring is available. Otherwise tokens are
kept in the keyring.
.TP
.I ~/.claude/.credentials.json
Claude Code's own login, read when you choose "Use my Claude Code login".
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects
Claude Code session transcripts, read locally for context window usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Overrides Claude Code's configuration directory (default \fI~/.claude\fR).
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/YigitSalihEmecen/claude-usage-on-menu-bar/issues
.PP
This is an unofficial app, not affiliated with or endorsed by Anthropic. It reads an
undocumented endpoint that may change without notice.
